    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299-a1">

                <pb facs="0680" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg632"/>

                <head>No. 1.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Government Office</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-01-18">18<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                day of</hi> 12<hi rendition="#italic">th month, at</hi> 12 <hi
                                rendition="#italic">noon,</hi> (12<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                January,</hi> 1868.)</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>We are authorized by the governor of Kanagawa to publish the following
                    information:</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Notification.</hi></p>
                <p>Intelligence having been roceived to the effect that a band of robbers, assembled
                    on a mountain near Oghino, in the province of Soshiu, at a distance of about ten
                    ri from Yokohama, had burnt a camp (ginya) belonging to Okubo Idsumo-no-kami and
                    killed his retainers; and that the said robbers also intended to visit Yokohama.
                    Itow Iwaitshiro, a vice-governor, had been sent to that place in command of a
                    detachment of troops in order to attack the robbers, on whose approach the
                    latter fled in the direction of Negoyamura and Hashimo-to-mura.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
